\[ x = 0.3252525\ldots \]
To eliminate the repeating part, we multiply \( x \) by 100 (since the repeating part starts after one decimal place):
\[ 100x = 32.5252525\ldots \]
Now, we also multiply \( x \) by 10 (since the repeating part is two digits long):
\[ 10x = 3.252525\ldots \]
Next, we subtract the second equation from the first equation:
\[ 100x - 10x = 32.5252525\ldots - 3.252525\ldots \]
This simplifies to:
\[ 90x = 29.27 \]
